cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A Narrative Introduction to Probability, Probabilistic Machine Learning, and Probabilistic Computing"
message: "If you use this textbook in teaching or research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Austerweil
    given-names: Joseph L.
    # NOTE (Joe): add your ORCID here — orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"
repository-code: "https://github.com/josephausterweil/probintro"
url: "https://josephausterweil.github.io/probintro/"
abstract: >-
  A free, open, interactive textbook that teaches probability, probabilistic
  machine learning, and probabilistic computing from a light background, told
  as one continuous narrative (the Chiba Tech mascot "Chibany" and a year of
  bento mysteries). It spans discrete probability through Bayesian learning,
  structured and sequential inference, decision theory and reinforcement
  learning, model complexity, deep networks and LLMs (in-context learning as
  implicit hierarchical Bayes, taught as a live debate), and ML ethics,
  fairness, and alignment. Every chapter interleaves runnable, validated
  GenJAX/JAX code, interactive in-browser widgets, and a Colab capstone, and
  offers two guided reading tracks — a beginner probabilistic-ML path and a
  Bayesian-cognitive-science path — plus an in-page English/Japanese toggle.
keywords:
  - probability
  - Bayesian inference
  - probabilistic programming
  - GenJAX
  - probabilistic machine learning
  - Bayesian cognitive science
  - in-context learning
  - interactive textbook
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
